# Buffers each input polygon outward by the live obstacle_margin coverage_server
# is actually planning with (bufferRingOutward, coverage_planning.cpp) — the
# same growth every real coverage plan applies to a drawn obstacle hole. Read-
# only, stateless: for the GUI's toggleable "obstacle clearance preview" map
# overlay (docs/claude/codemaps/mowgli_coverage.md), never consumed by planning
# itself. buffered[i] corresponds to obstacles[i]; a degenerate input ring is
# echoed back unbuffered rather than dropped (mirrors bufferRingOutward).
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] obstacles
---
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] buffered
float64 obstacle_margin_m
